    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (71.87) and **Mickey Moniak** (71.22) anchor our offensive strategy as our premier starts. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a distinct advantage against Wrobleski; despite the platoon disadvantage, his efficiency is buoyed by his elite stolen base profile, with the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery providing an estimated +4% boost to his SB probability. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** thrives on a massive +14% platoon edge against McGreevy, making him a high-leverage target to drive run production from the #5 spot. **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) remains a primary play as well; even assuming a #3 hole, his massive +19% SP skill adjustment against V\u00e1squez suggests he is primed to exploit a favorable matchup despite potential park headwinds.\n\nOur toughest roster decision centered on **Cole Young** (40.82), who ultimately stayed on the bench. While his +8% boost from batting second and +2% bump for stolen base potential against Seymour make him a viable depth piece, he failed to surpass the efficiency threshold set by our incumbents. We are managing **Zach McKinstry** (41.23) and **Austin Riley** (43.54) with caution; **Zach McKinstry** faces the elite arm of Webb and is buried in the #9 slot, while **Austin Riley** draws a difficult matchup against the formidable Schlittler (2.91 xERA). We remain particularly cautious with **Josh Naylor** (43.69), whose utility is severely capped by a -15% penalty against Seymour\u2019s high-end skill set and a poor platoon split.\n\nMonitoring today's lineups is mandatory, specifically for **Isaac Paredes**, as our projection relies on an assumed #3 placement. While we are currently rostering **Gabriel Moreno** (57.98) and **Brice Turang** (55.00) as solid mid-tier producers, the shadow of our IL-stashed talent\u2014including **James Wood**, **Trevor Story**, and the absent **Jose Caballero**\u2014remains a concern for our total category output. With no major weather red flags, the focus remains on leveraging the speed of **Corbin Carroll** and the contact profile of **Mickey Moniak** to gain ground in the stolen base and RBI columns. We continue to hold **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** on the periphery, ready to rotate in should the late-game situational markers shift in our favor.",
